# ============================================================
# CRITICAL — species-at-risk location protection
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Boreal caribou are listed as Threatened. Nothing containing collection
# coordinates may ever enter this repository. These rules are a safety net,
# not the primary control: the primary control is
# scripts/13_build_public_dataset.R, which refuses to write a file that
# still carries a coordinate-like column.
#
# If you add a new data file, check it against data/DATA_DICTIONARY.md
# before committing.
# ============================================================

# The raw dataset — contains Latitude/Longitude. NEVER commit.
All_data_updated.csv
*_backup*.csv
*_pre_dedup*.csv

# Anything with coordinates in the name
*coordinates*
*coords*
*latlon*
*_gps*

# Distance-source spatial layers (large, and geolocate the study animals)
*.geojson
*.gpkg
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.prj
*.cpg
*.sbn
*.sbx

# Large rasters — download separately, see README
*.tif
*.tiff
*.7z

# Road layer caches built by 00b_road_layers.R
roads_winter.gpkg
roads_allseason.gpkg

# Per-sample distance tables (row order maps back to collection sites)
AllSeasonRoad_distances.csv

# Serialised mgcv model objects. gam() stores its MODEL FRAME inside the
# fitted object, so any model containing s(x_proj, y_proj) carries the full
# coordinate table — m$model$x_proj recovers every collection location in
# two lines of R. Publish the .txt summaries and rendered surfaces instead.
*.rds
outputs/models/

# ============================================================
# Ordinary R / OS noise
# ============================================================
.RData
.RDataTmp*
.Rhistory
.Rproj.user/
.Rproj
*.Rproj
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
_docx_tmp/
_staged.docx
